@title Extending and Customizing Phorge
@group extensions
@order 10


Guide to making Phorge better for your team.

Overview
========

Phorge is targeting mostly professional teams, and these teams often want things
done in a particular way. Since different teams want different things, Phorge
cannot be that thing for everybody.
Instead, the way to make Phorge be perfect for your team is by //extending// it:
adding code to suite your needs.


Fundamentals
============

Phorge primarily discovers functionality by looking at concrete subclasses
of some base class. For example, @{article:Configuring Custom Fields |adding a
field to Tasks} can be done by adding a class that extends
`ManiphestCustomField`.

Whenever a feature is needed, we find all the implementations, instantiate each
of them, and check each one if it applies to the current scenario.

Existing Extensions
===================

Using the magic of the Community, there are already a few extensions already
made available by people who needed them. Some can be found in the Wiki at
[[ https://we.phorge.it/w/community_resources/ | Community Resources ]], and
some are harder to find. The [[ https://we.phorge.it/w/docs/extensions/install |
How to Install Extensions ]] page can guide you in how to instal them.


What You Can Extend And Invoke
==============================

In general, we try to make everything extensible. Some examples:
- Adding @{article:Configuring Custom Fields | custom fields} (properties) to
  common objects
- Remarkup (rich text) formatting rules
- Authentication providers
- Rendering documents (under Files and under Diffusion)
- Adding new applications

Documentation about extension points can be found in individual manual sections,
and non-documented extensions can usually be found by reading the code of
similar items. If it's unclear whether something is extensible, or how to extend
it, feel free to ask in
[[https://we.phorge.it/ponder/question/create/ | Ponder]].


Next Steps
==========

Continue by:

  - visiting the [[ https://we.phorge.it/w/community_resources/ |
    Community Resources ]] page to find existing extensions and
    libraries.
  - check out the [[ https://we.phorge.it/w/docs/extensions/ |
    Extensions documents ]] in the Wiki for
    information about writing, distributing and finding extensions.
  - reading in @{article:Adding New Classes} on the technical aspects
    of extending your install.
  - reading [[ /book/contrib | Phorge Contributor Documentation]] for details
    about code-style, work-style, and contributing to the upstream.
